[Music]  okay everybody so this is my spoiler  free review of house of gucci this film  is directed by ridley scott and it has  an all-star cast in lady gaga adam  driver jeremy irons jared leto and al  pacino now this is a film  while i was watching it i really enjoyed  it i thought it was excellent and it is  also a film that when i left the theater  and i was walking back to my apartment  thinking about it  i liked it  less and less and that doesn't mean i  disliked it i just liked it less because  what i realized the main thing about  this film it's the main point i'm gonna  make about this film is a perfect  example where everything is done so well  in this film it's it's near perfect that  it's execution and it's amazing how  entertaining it was for such a long run  time of two hours and 38 minutes i was  engaged the whole time  but  i didn't feel anything from it it was  super cold but maybe yeah you could say  this is a story about the gucci family  right these are some cold calculated  people we meet but it still has to give  me some kind of emotional feeling  watching it especially in the end and i  didn't feel that here at all i felt like  it had strong relationships in the film  it had a really good story  but again  it's something that's just an  entertaining watch but it doesn't stay  with you i don't didn't make me think at  all um  and i yeah i never felt emotional at all  in this film i didn't feel in any sense  of form something where you could feel  sad for someone or feel this like a  powerful feeling to it or anything like  that it just felt like a well done film  that's an enjoyable ride but there's not  much else to it and that's what really  stops this film from being a classic for  me um but  the positives that you're gonna see in  this film is  lady gaga's performance is great  i wouldn't say it's worthy of an oscar  but i think it's worthy of an oscar  nomination for sure but  that's like most of this film is  everything gets the job done you know  and  it's expected al pacino jeremy irons  they just bring it here adam driver does  great but doesn't have to really do much  in this performance it's a very straight  role for him and ridley scott same thing  with his directing a lot of his camera  choices are great but again it's more a  laid-back  reserved  statement by the director on this film  and how he's shooting it which made  sense for the film so you're not really  kind of getting to see ridley scott or  adam driver really do their thing  because it's not really required here  but the standout for me is jared leto i  thought that  his character stole the show every time  he was on screen  the prosthetics on him are game changing  i mean this was one of the best makeup  jobs i have seen to date and it gets me  excited for what's to come because i  really never felt like i was watching  somebody in  makeup so that was really awesome it  felt like a different person than jared  leto and props to him his performance is  stellar the other thing about this movie  is it does cover a lot of ground it  covers a lot of time in this story about  the gucci's and  it feels sometimes rushed in its  transition to time  in this  huge story it's going for  which is bizarre in such a long run time  that it feels rushed at points there's  some certain time jumps that feel  really just like whoa hold on a second  where are we what just happened and was  that earned that's definitely a critique  i have but i think if you see this  trailer and this is your cup of tea you  like this type of genre this mood the  silliness that's also in this i think  you're gonna love this film if it's like  something you expected to like you're  gonna like it if this isn't your cup of  tea i still think you're gonna enjoy it  but like i said  it's where i'm at where i just didn't  feel anything from it and every movie i  want to feel something right that's  that's the main point of film is to get  a feeling out of you relate to people  but you know maybe it's a bias take by  me but i really just didn't feel  anything at all and i felt like  the story was so focused on being a  strong story and getting the information  right and it runs so much like a  documentary but i think it just forgot  the part of wait a minute am i feeling  anything from these big moments i'm  supposed to feel because i i just felt  cold i didn't feel anything about these  characters i can't really talk in depth  why or what certain characters i felt a  certain way about because it would be  spoilers but  that's what i'm going to say with my  spoiler free taking it i'm giving this  film an 8.5 i think it's definitely  worth a watch it's coming out in two  days  but  lower expectations and  you're really watching it to see a  well-executed film with some really  awesome acting performances but again  i'm not thinking about it anymore i'm  ready to move on it's not sticking with  me like if you watch my review for the  movie spencer that's the example it's  the opposite effect where spencer i  liked more and more as i thought about  it and how it stuck with me and hit me  emotionally so it's missing that here  for it to even be considered for some  kind of award like best picture i just  don't think it's anywhere near that  class but  let me know if you plan on seeing it let  me know if you're excited for it and let  me know when you do watch what you  thought i'd love to hear your thoughts i  read every comment try to respond as  many as i can  and you can reach out to me anywhere  tell me what you thought of any film i'd  love to hear it and please make sure  that you check out steve varley show on  twitter instagram and tick tock for more  of me i share clips there i also do  celebrity interviews you're gonna see  those and if you really like what i do  here i would really appreciate if you  could sign up for a membership that will  help me do this full time one day and  you get special perks as well and i'll  see you next time

